Q2c Does the downstream peak track the stop codon or the 3' fill edge?

  3396 transcripts; downstream fill ends at offset 33 to 499 (median 499)

  common search range +1..+499: 2737 of 3396 transcripts reach it (659 dropped, and they are the short ones)
    every eligible transcript ends at 499 — no length contrast left to stratify on

  common search range +1..+499: 2737 of 3396 transcripts reach it (659 dropped, and they are the short ones)
    every eligible transcript ends at 499 — no length contrast left to stratify on

  Both strata now search the same offsets. A peak at the same offset
  in both is anchored on the stop codon; a peak that shifts with the
  stratum's own fill extent is 3' UTR length.
